WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.010
Selling to Dennis and Gloria draws extra scrutiny.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:07.526
Maryland’s Medicare supplement rules require advertising to be filed with the Insurance

00:00:07.526 --> 00:00:12.042
Commissioner before use and prohibit cold lead devices, which are mailings that

00:00:12.042 --> 00:00:16.558
hide their insurance purpose, high-pressure tactics, and any suggestion of government endorsement.

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:19.568
Twisting, misrepresentation and the use of titles implying

00:00:19.568 --> 00:00:22.579
Medicare expertise beyond a producer license are banned.

00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:27.471
Producers must make reasonable efforts to determine that a policy is appropriate: it

00:00:27.471 --> 00:00:32.363
may not duplicate Medicare, an Advantage plan or another supplement, and it may

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:36.502
not be sold to someone on Medicaid except in narrow cases.

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:38.760
Excessive insurance is itself a violation.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.979
At application the producer delivers the federal buyer’s guide, Choosing a Medigap Policy, and

00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:48.824
an outline of coverage that summarizes benefits and premiums in a standard format.

00:00:48.824 --> 00:00:53.670
Maryland gives the applicant 30 days after delivery to return the policy for

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:58.516
a full refund, and that right must appear prominently on the first page.

00:00:58.516 --> 00:01:02.989
If the sale replaces another supplement, a replacement notice is signed, the

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:07.462
application asks about existing coverage, and the new insurer must credit the

00:01:07.462 --> 00:01:11.935
time already served under the old policy, waiving pre-existing condition, waiting, elimination

00:01:11.935 --> 00:01:15.290
and probationary periods for benefits the old policy covered.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:20.568
A Maryland supplement must provide at least the federally required minimum benefits,

00:01:20.568 --> 00:01:25.846
and its deductible and coinsurance benefits must change automatically when Medicare changes,

00:01:25.846 --> 00:01:30.684
so Dennis never finds a gap opened by a January adjustment.

00:01:30.684 --> 00:01:36.841
A policy may not duplicate benefits Medicare already pays, may not use exclusions or

00:01:36.841 --> 00:01:42.999
limitations stricter than Medicare’s, and may not be offered at an unapproved introductory rate.

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:48.716
It may not be canceled or nonrenewed except for nonpayment or material misrepresentation,

00:01:48.716 --> 00:01:54.434
and a spouse’s coverage may not end merely because the insured’s coverage ends.

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:59.272
If the insured becomes eligible for Medicaid, benefits and premiums are

00:01:59.272 --> 00:02:03.670
suspended for up to 24 months at the insured’s request.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:08.087
A Maryland supplement may exclude a pre-existing condition for no more than six

00:02:08.087 --> 00:02:12.504
months, and may define one no more strictly than a condition for which

00:02:12.504 --> 00:02:16.580
a physician gave advice or treatment in the six months before coverage.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.658
Time spent under qualifying prior health coverage can shorten that waiting period.

00:02:20.658 --> 00:02:24.055
When one supplement replaces another, the applicant gets credit for

00:02:24.055 --> 00:02:27.113
time already served for benefits the old policy covered.

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:31.530
Compensation rules protect buyers from churning: a producer’s first-year commission may not exceed

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.946
200 percent of the renewal commission, renewal commissions must continue for a set

00:02:35.946 --> 00:02:40.363
number of years, and a replacement sale earns only the renewal rate, so

00:02:40.363 --> 00:02:44.440
there is no bonus for moving Gloria from one supplement to another.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:48.871
Beyond the federal six-month open enrollment at 65, Maryland adds protections.

00:02:48.871 --> 00:02:54.511
People under 65 who qualify for Medicare because of disability must be offered Plans

00:02:54.511 --> 00:03:00.150
A and D for six months after Part B enrollment, and the Plan A

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.984
premium may not exceed the average paid by policyholders 65 and older.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:09.818
Since July 1, 2023, Maryland has a birthday rule: for 30 days

00:03:09.818 --> 00:03:14.652
after each birthday, an existing policyholder may switch to a policy with

00:03:14.652 --> 00:03:19.486
equal or lesser benefits from any insurer without underwriting, and insurers must

00:03:19.486 --> 00:03:24.320
give notice of that right 30 to 60 days before the birthday.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:29.960
Group supplements that end must offer individual conversion, and continuation applies when membership ends.

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:33.855
Medicare SELECT is a Medigap policy with a network.

00:03:33.855 --> 00:03:39.049
For full benefits the insured must use the plan’s network hospitals and

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:43.810
sometimes physicians, except in emergencies, in exchange for a lower premium.

00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:46.840
Benefits are otherwise the standard lettered plan.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:52.467
A SELECT policyholder has the right to switch to the insurer’s standard version

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:58.093
of the same or a lesser plan without underwriting if she moves out

00:03:58.093 --> 00:04:03.287
of the network area or at any time during a stated window.

00:04:03.287 --> 00:04:08.048
Theo explains to Gloria that SELECT saves money only if her

00:04:08.048 --> 00:04:12.809
hospital is in the network, and that the Maryland rules in

00:04:12.809 --> 00:04:17.570
this lesson apply to SELECT as fully as to any supplement.
